A||||5||Robert||So I dragged this Fiero owner form the Pontiac Dealership……..||||10||
Z||000000||Robert||06-30-2000||07:18 PM||||As some of you know, I live close enough to my work so I can ride my bicycle.  I pass the local Pontiac dealership on my ride (the one mentioned on my web page as breaking stuff on my car).  Well the other day I’m headed home for lunch when I see a Gold 86 GT fastback in the parking lot, with the owner and a parts guy looking at the quarter windows.  I couldn’t resist stopping an asking about the car.  The owner (Bill) said he was looking to replace the cracked windows.  That parts guy didn’t have a clue what a Fiero was, let alone how the find the window.  I told them both about George at the Fiero Shop, and how he sells the quarter windows for under a $100 each.  The parts guy then said I knew way more about Fiero’s than he did, and left.  I gave Bill George’s business card and told him to give him a call.  We started talking Fiero stuff and I asked him if he had some spare time, he might want to come over to my place and see my Fiero.  He followed me home, and was impressed with my car.  We talked for near an hour about Fiero’s and cars in general.   He bought his car 3 years ago from the second owner, with only 51,000 miles on it.  His engine is way cleaner than mine, with quite a few upgrades.  Bill’s not online, so I couldn’t point him to any web sites.  I think he will soon be a member of the Golden Gate Fiero’s, if George has anything to say about it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
